        "original_id": "d1eb1f88-c788-5beb-a266-ea6b4f123873",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Brian Olsen, Mike Kyle, Frank Fertitta III, Lorenzo Fertitta\n- Companies: Zuffa, Station Casinos, Semaphore Entertainment Group\n- Organizations: WEC, Ultimate Fighting Championship\n- Events: WEC 20\n- Concepts: WEC Heavyweight Championship, organizational purchase, title abolition\n\nFacts:\n- In January 2001, Zuffa was founded in Las Vegas, Nevada, by Station Casinos executives Frank Fertitta III and Lorenzo Fertitta to serve as the parent entity of the Ultimate Fighting Championship after they bought the UFC from Semaphore Entertainment Group.\n- At WEC 20, the main event was a heavyweight bout between Brian Olsen and Mike Kyle.\n- Brian Olsen was the last WEC Heavyweight Champion before the title was abolished when Zuffa purchased the organization.",
